{{Quote|Morgan Elsbeth had factories on Corellia.''"<br />"''Her Imperial operation should have been dismantled after the Rebellion.|Ahsoka Tano and Hera Syndulla discuss Morgan Elsbeth's operations|<ref name="Part Two" />}}
'''Facility 301G''' was an [[factory|industrial facility]] on the [[planet]] [[Corellia]]'s [[Santhe Shipyards]]. It was owned by industrialist [[Morgan Elsbeth]], who used it to manufacture and refurbish [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[capital ship]] [[hyperdrive]] cores. Following the [[Galactic Concordance|fall]] of the Galactic Empire, the facility passed to the [[New Republic]] under the control of [[Regional Supervisor]] [[Myn Weaver]].

In [[9 ABY]], Elsbeth tasked the shipyards with secretly manufacturing the hyperdrive for the [[extragalactic]] [[starship]] prototype ''[[Eye of Sion]]'', which she would use to rescue [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]] from his exile in the [[far galaxy]]. The shipyard's secret [[Morgan Elsbeth's forces|Imperial sympathizer]] presence was discovered by former [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] and [[New Republic]] [[General]] [[Hera Syndulla]] during an investigation of Elsbeth's activities, leading to the arrest of Weaver and his staff by the [[New Republic army]].

==Description==
{{Quote|This was one of Morgan's facilities. She supplied raw materials used in the construction of hyperdrive generators for ''Imperial''-class Star Destroyers. Now we take them apart, using the cores to power the new ships in the Defense Fleet.|Supervisor Weaver describes Facility 301G's operations|<ref name="Part Two" />}}
[[File:Facility_301G_Part_2.png|thumb|240x240px|The factory floor of Facility 301G during the New Republic era]]
Facility 301G<ref name="Rise">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref> was a large [[ocean|seaside]] [[factory|facility]]<ref name="Part Two" /> located in [[Coronet City]]'s<ref name="Official Guide" /> [[Santhe Shipyards]].<ref name="Rise" /> It consisted of an open-[[atmosphere|air]] [[hangar|docking yard]] for [[transport]]s and a long covered depot where [[hyperdrive]] cores were assembled using raw materials arranged in piles throughout. A wide corridor in the middle of the assembly line allowed [[technician|workers]] and staff to traverse the facility<ref name="Part Two" />  using [[REV-2K personnel carrier]]<ref name="Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> [[speeder]]s, while large cranes covered the roof.<ref name="Part Two" /> 

The entire site was controlled from a central control room overseeing the docking yard. During the [[New Republic Era]], the room was staffed by both [[human]] and [[protocol droid]] operators, with humans fulfilling air traffic control duties and the [[droid]]s overseeing the production line and logistics. A number of [[computer]] terminals were arranged below a large [[viewport]] on the yard side of the room, while [[memory bank]]s and servers covered the other.<ref name="Part Two" />

==History==
===Imperial Era===
[[File:Imperial-class_hyperdrive_cores.png|left|thumb|Two hyperdrive cores for ''Imperial''-class Star Destroyers, under construction in Elsbeth's facility|250x250px]]
During the [[Imperial Era]], [[Magistrate]]<ref name="Part Two" /> and [[Nightsisters|Nightsister]] [[witch]]<ref name="Path of Fear">{{TOTE|The Path of Fear}}</ref> [[Morgan Elsbeth]], one of [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]]'s closest allies, maintained a number of [[shipyard]]s across [[the galaxy]], manufacturing [[starship]]s for the [[Imperial Navy]]. One of them, based on the [[planet]] [[Corellia]], supplied raw materials which were used to construct hyperdrive generators for the [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial''-class Star Destroyer]]s<ref name="Part Two" /> constructed in the planet's [[atmosphere|orbit]].<ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> The facility was staffed by a number of contractors loyal to Elsbeth, as well as occasional Imperial fanatics.<ref name="Part Two" /> The facility was also logged in the [[Imperial Archives]] under the section of "Corellian Infrastructure".<ref name="Rise" />

===Dissolution and operation under the New Republic===
{{Quote|When the Empire fell, all Imperial assets were dissolved and redistributed, including those held by Morgan Elsbeth.|Supervisor Weaver|<ref name="Part Two" />}}
[[File:Myn_weaver.png|thumb|275x275px|Supervisor Myn Weaver was tasked with overseeing the transition of the facility to New Republic control]]
At some point following the [[Galactic Concordance|end]] of the [[Galactic Civil War]] and the formation of the [[New Republic]], the shipyard, along with all Imperial military assets was dissolved and redistributed to the new government for re-assignment.<ref name="Part Two" /> By [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Ahsokadate">{{AhsokaSeriesDate}}</ref> although most of the workers and administrative staff remained the same,<ref name="Rise" /> [[Regional Supervisor]] [[Myn Weaver]] was tasked with overseeing the operations of the facility during its transitional phase, where it was tasked with dismantling the hyperdrive cores still present in the factory and rebuilding them for use on board [[New Republic Defense Fleet]] vessels. Scraps and useless equipment from the leftover starships were sold to the shipyard's wealthy investors, and the profits were used for New Republic reconstruction projects, among other things. Alongside Weaver, a board of directors oversaw the commercial aspects of the shipyards and had first looks at all unique hardware discovered within the ships, their price points and their distribution. According to Weaver, a single [[Star Destroyer]] was enough to fund multiple of these operations.<ref name="Part Two" />

Despite the New Republic's efforts to best control leftover Imperial military assets, the lack of experienced personnel meant that, at least initially,<ref name="Rise" /> those of Elsbeth's Imperial workers<ref name="Part Two" /> judged to be of low risk and low value by New republic Intelligence staff were allowed to continue working in the shipyard under the process of de-Imperialization<ref name="Rise" /> despite not having been vetted or loyal to the new government. Weaver believed that they only cared for their payment, and that they lacked focus for the nuances of galactic politics, so completely trusted them. This led to the development of an underground network of Imperial remnants' spies in the shipyards, including Elsbeth's very own.<ref name="Part Two" />

===A secret project===
{{Quote|Do the facilities still employ any of ''[Elsbeth's]'' former staff?''"<br />"''Of course, there is no other way to remain operational. An Empire doesn't just become a Republic overnight.|Ahsoka Tano questions Weaver on the workers' loyalty|<ref name="Part Two" />}}
[[File:MarrokandAhsokaCorellia.png|thumb|240x240px|Ahsoka confronts Marrok in the facility's dock|left]]
Around 9 ABY,<ref name="Ahsokadate" /> Elsbeth, with the help of ex-[[Jedi]] [[Baylan Skoll]] and his apprentice [[Shin Hati]] discovered the existence of a starmap that contained the details of the [[Pathway to Peridea]], an ancient route to a [[Far galaxy|galaxy]] neighboring her [[the galaxy|own]]. Believing the destination of the Pathway to be the location where her former ally Thrawn was stranded after the [[Liberation of Lothal]]<ref name="Part Two" /> in [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> Elsbeth tasked Skoll and Hati with acquiring the map, and secretly began constructing an extragalactic transportation vessel named the ''[[Eye of Sion]]'' above the planet [[Seatos]] which she believed to be the beginning of the Path. To equip the vessel with enough power for the trip, Elsbeth tasked her spies working in her old shipyards with acquiring and shipping [[Super Star Destroyer]] hyperdrives to her under the guise of a classified New Republic Defence Force project; indeed the shipyards produced nine refurbished engine cores without anyone noticing, with Elsbeth's [[HK-87 assassin droid]]s preventing the facility's [[protocol droid]]s from taking a closer look.<ref name="Part Two" />

Despite the precautions, former [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] and New Republic [[General]] [[Hera Syndulla]] noticed Elsbeth's suspicious activities and visited Corellia to inspect the facility. During their tour, Syndulla noticed the tenth and final hyperdrive being loaded into [[transport CT-O5]] and questioned Weaver on its purpose, knowing that the Defense Fleet's starships did not require that much power. Coming upon the project's classified file, Syndulla questioned droid [[C1-D1]] on the authority required to unseal it, only for the unit to testify on the HK-87 droids lurking about the facility and ordering them not to engage with the project. Realizing the ruse, Syndulla ordered the control center to ground CT-05, forcing the spies stationed there to confront her.<ref name="Part Two" />

===Discovery and detentions===
{{Quote|How can they still be loyal to the Empire?''"<br />"''It's not loyalty. It's greed.|Hera Syndulla and Ahsoka Tano following the battle|<ref name="Part Two" />}}
[[File:Phantom_II-ToilAndTrouble.png|thumb|Transport CT-O5 mange to escape with the hyperdrive.|250x250px]]
Syndulla and Tano engaged the Imperials, who drew their [[blaster]]s and fired at them, killing and injuring many of the conspirators as well as several protocol droids. Syndulla then took off in her personal modified [[Sheathipede-class transport shuttle|''Sheathipede''-class transport shuttle]] ''[[Phantom II]]'', managing to reach CT-05 just in time for her [[astromech droid]] [[C1-10P|"Chopper"]] to plant a [[homing beacon]] on it, while Tano engaged Elsbeth's forces, including<ref name="Part Two" /> the former [[Inquisitor]]<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> [[Marrok]] and several HK-87s on the ground.<ref name="Part Two" />

Despite destroying the droids and injuring Marrok, Tano was held back from reaching the [[transport]] and was forced to retreat. Following the battle, [[New Republic army]] troopers arrived at the facility and detained the Imperial sympahizers left behind, including Manager Weaver.<ref name="Part Two" /> 

===Legacy===
{{Quote|One of the most serious examples of Imperial-driven sabotage could be found on the shipyards of Corellia that had previously been administered by the Imperial industrialist Morgan Elsbeth.|Beaumont Kin in his book ''The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire''|<ref name="Rise" />}}
[[Historian]] [[Beaumont Kin]] mentioned the facility in<ref name="Rise" /> his<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> post-[[First Order-Resistance War|war]] [[book]] ''[[The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''<ref name="Rise" /> published in [[35 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{RiseAndFallDate}}</ref> where he described the New Republic's failure to detect Elsbeth's forces within it as "one of the most serious examples of Imperial-driven sabotage".<ref name="Rise" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Facility301GConcept-Ahsoka.png|thumb|240px|Concept art of the facility by Brett Northcutt]]
Facility 301G first appeared in [[Part Two: Toil and Trouble]], the second episode of the [[Star Wars: Ahsoka|''Ahsoka'' TV series']] [[Ahsoka Season 1|first season]],<ref name="Part Two" /> which aired on [[August 22]], [[2023]] on [[Disney+]].<ref name="New Release Date">{{SW|url=news/ahsoka-new-premiere-date|text=''Ahsoka'' Premiere Moves Up to Tuesday, August 22|date=2023-08-18|quote=The two-episode premiere of ''Ahsoka'' will now arrive on Tuesday, August 22 at 6 p.m. PT on Disney+}}</ref> It was identified as Facility 301G in the book ''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]'' by Dr. [[Chris Kempshall]] which was published in [[2024]].<ref name="Rise" />

